This patch is needed because several Codex TUI terminal assumptions do not
hold on Solaris PTYs and older terminal environments.

What it does:
- replaces the default crossterm event stream with a Solaris stdin reader
- avoids terminal capability probes and keyboard modes that proved unreliable on Solaris
- prefers ASCII-safe prompts and separators on older terminals
- keeps startup and inline rendering on the safer non-alt-screen path where needed

Why it is needed:
- without it, the Solaris TUI can miss input, stall during startup, or render
  poorly in terminals commonly used on Solaris systems

